.TH OSX 1
.SH NAME
osx \- safe, JSON-first macOS subsystem utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B osx
[--apply] [--duration DURATION] SUBSYSTEM ACTION [ARGUMENTS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs a focused set of macOS-native utilities without invoking a shell. Results
are emitted as versioned JSON. Read-only operations run normally; an operation
that changes system state requires the explicit \fB--apply\fR flag.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B osx defaults read com.apple.finder AppleShowAllFiles
.br
.B osx defaults write com.apple.finder AppleShowAllFiles bool true --apply
.br
.B osx caffeinate start --duration 45m --apply
.SH SUBSYSTEMS
info show; battery status; power settings; network quality or interfaces;
Spotlight search; LaunchServices opening; DNS status or flush; security
FileVault, Gatekeeper, firewall, or SIP; updates list or install; defaults
read, write, or delete; speech; clipboard read or write; ditto copies; AppleScript file
execution; volume get, set, mute, or unmute; and caffeinate start.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 for invalid usage, and 4 for a rejected or failed native operation.
